DateStrip takes daysWithMatches (a set of day keys). Days with fixtures show
a 2px muted dot; the selected chip shows nothing (the volt fill is already
the marker) and today keeps its 4px volt dot. Matches computes the set from
the matches payload using DateStrip's own exported dayKey, so the dot can
never disagree with the chip it sits on.

